{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ConjRhoPrefactorStructural","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ConjRhoPrefactorStructural","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.rho_eq_qdim_via_canonical_knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.rho_eq_qdim_via_canonical_knot","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L247-L282","doc":"**ρ rule as a corollary of the canonical-knot-id (closure path\nfor GAP-A-4).**\n\nOnce GAP-A-1's `CanonicalKnotIdSDP` instance is established for\na given nucleus, the SDP multiplicity ρ is *uniquely determined*\nby the canonical T_w via the Wedderburn dominant-summand\nformula: ρ = [d_{λ*(T_w)}]_q.\n\nPR #608's `r5-full-canonical-knot-solver.witness.json` records\nthe per-Wedderburn-block min-eigenvalue per candidate; the\ndominant summand λ* is the one that achieves the minimum\nα-gap (or, equivalently, contributes the largest |y_λ · χ_λ|\nin the Frobenius factorisation).\n\nFor the witnessed cases the multiplicity is:\n* `helium3`: ρ_star = 3  (per witness `winner.rho_star`).\n* `deuterium`: ρ_star = 3 at the prototype's L=8 winner\n  (σ_2 σ_1^6 σ_2^{-1}); the historical assignment ρ = 1\n  remains tied to the historical 6_2 knot, which fails the\n  single-term cost.  The discrepancy resolves only after\n  multi-term cost wiring (PR #608 followup #1) lands.\n* `tritium`: deferred (Hoefsmit at H_5 pending).\n\nThis theorem closes GAP-A-4 *conditional on* GAP-A-1 closure\n(which the helium3 theorem in `conj-canonical-knot-id-sdp.lean`\ndischarges given a strict-complementarity certificate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.n0_eq_3_ZpN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.n0_eq_3_ZpN","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L233-L234","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instRhoPrefactorStructural_helium3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instRhoPrefactorStructural_helium3","kind":"instance","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L213-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instRhoPrefactorStructural_tritium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instRhoPrefactorStructural_tritium","kind":"instance","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L197-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instRhoPrefactorStructural_deuterium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instRhoPrefactorStructural_deuterium","kind":"instance","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L181-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.q_int_placeholder_correct_at_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.q_int_placeholder_correct_at_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L160-L172","doc":"**Categorical correctness of the placeholder at the classical limit.**\nAt `q = 1`, the q-integer `[n]_q` collapses to `n` (since\n`(q^n - q^{-n})/(q - q^{-1}) → n` as q → 1). Since `ρ = d_λ*` for\neach particle at the classical limit, the placeholder\n`q_int_placeholder := fun _ => ρ` correctly equals `[d_λ*]_1`\niff `ρ = d_λ*`. The instances below have `ρ = rho` and the\n`rho_eq_qdim_placeholder` is discharged vacuously for general q —\nbut ONLY at q=1 is this the true categorical statement. Promoting\nto a non-vacuous q-bracket formula for q ≠ 1 is Phase 1c work\n(audit #5 follow-up; needs Mathlib `qInt` lemma in scope). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hook_length_6_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hook_length_6_3","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L144-L149","doc":"**Hook-length formula derivation: d_λ((6,3) ⊢ 9) = 48.**\nHook lengths: `[7, 6, 5, 3, 2, 1, 3, 2, 1]` (row 1: positions\n1-6; row 2: positions 1-3). Hook product:\n`7·6·5·3·2·1·3·2·1 = 7560`. SYT count: `9! / 7560 = 48`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hook_length_8_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hook_length_8_1","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L137-L142","doc":"**Hook-length formula derivation: d_λ((8,1) ⊢ 9) = 8.**\nHook lengths: `[9, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 1]` (row 1: 8 cells;\nrow 2: 1 cell). Hook product: `9·7·6·5·4·3·2·1·1 = 45360`.\nSYT count: `9! / 45360 = 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hook_length_5_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hook_length_5_1","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L130-L135","doc":"**Hook-length formula derivation: d_λ((5,1) ⊢ 6) = 5.**\nHook lengths for the (5, 1) Young diagram are\n`[6, 4, 3, 2, 1, 1]` (row 1: positions 1-5; row 2: position 1).\nHook product: `6·4·3·2·1·1 = 144`. SYT count: `6! / 144 = 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.rho_eq_qdim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.rho_eq_qdim","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L100-L100","doc":"`ρ = round([d_λ*]_q)` — the SDP multiplicity equals the nearest\npositive integer to the q-deformed dominant SYT count.  Encoded\nas an inequality: the real distance from `(rho : ℝ)` to\n`q_int d_lambda_star` is at most ½. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.q_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.q_int","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The q-integer `[n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n}) / (q - q^{-1})` evaluated at\nthe natural number `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.d_lambda_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.d_lambda_pos","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.d_lambda_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.d_lambda_star","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The dominant Young diagram in the Wedderburn decomposition\n(encoded as the size `d_lambda` of its SYT count); derived\nstructurally as argmax_{λ ⊢ n₀} |y_λ(q) · χ_λ(T_w)|.  Per\n`binding-k-solver.witness.json`: deuteron's dominant λ* = (5,1)\nhas d_λ = 5; tritium's λ* = (8,1) has d_λ = 8; helium-3's\nλ* = (6,3) has d_λ = 48. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.rho_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.rho_pos","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.rho","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The SDP multiplicity ρ for the confined particle at `(Z, N, q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.n₀_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.n₀_eq","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Sanity: the strand count is exactly `3 * (Z + N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.n₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.n₀","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Atomic strand count `n₀ = 3 * (Z + N)` (the Hecke-algebra rank\nin which the canonical T_w is to be Wedderburn-decomposed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.A_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.A_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Atomic mass number A = Z + N; positive (so n₀ is well-defined). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RhoPrefactorStructural","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.lean#L52-L100","doc":"**RhoPrefactorStructural** — the conjectural class.\n\nIndexed by `(Z, N, q)` (proton count, neutron count, substrate\nparameter) — using `(Z, N)` rather than `A = Z + N` alone\nDISAMBIGUATES isobars (same A, different (Z,N)): tritium (Z=1, N=2)\nand helium-3 (Z=2, N=1) both have A=3 and would otherwise overlap\nas instances per Copilot's PR #614 review.\n\nAsserts that the SDP multiplicity `ρ` is derivable as the (rounded)\nquantum dimension of the dominant Wedderburn summand of the\ncanonical Hecke element at the *atomic* strand count\n$n_0 = 3 \\cdot (Z + N)$.\n\nThe atomic-strand-count specialisation is **structurally required**:\nproton (Z=1, N=0) and ³He (Z=2, N=1) have *identical* Wedderburn\nstructure at the braid strand count (3) but distinct ρ — the\nembedding into H_{3(Z+N)} is what carries the multiplicity\ninformation.  Numerical evidence:\n`computations/rho-prefactor-structural-verifier.witness.json`\n+ `binding-k-solver.witness.json` (issue #604 deliverables 3 + 4). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:rho-prefactor-structural","label":"conj:rho-prefactor-structural","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-rho-prefactor-structural.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}